/* UTIL's trigonometry and latitude tables, as X-macro lists of typed values.  Each list is
 * expanded in util_math.c by a macro that emits one entry in the form its table needs
 * (little-endian bytes into fs98_util_data, or the Q16 words of fs98_util_cos_q16).
 * C99 cannot evaluate cos/atan/asin in a static initialiser, so the numbers stay; each is
 * an exact function of its index except the exceptions named below, which retail
 * stores one unit away from the correctly rounded value.  Retail's offsets are into
 * UTIL's .data; the build checks the whole image against retail (tools/check_data_image.py,
 * row UTIL, at=_fs98_util_data), so a mistyped value fails the build.
 *
 * UTIL_COS_Q32     +0x0f4, 129 entries i = 0..128, Q32 cosine of the angle i/512 of a turn:
 *                  min(0xffffffff, trunc(2^32 cos(pi i / 256))).
 * UTIL_ASIN1       +0x2f8, 61 entries i = 0..60, Q15 turns of asin(i/64), round(asin(i/64)
 *                  * 0x8000 / pi); except i = 54, which is 10474 (rounding gives 10475).
 * UTIL_ASIN2       +0x372, 29 entries: the first 12 are asin((241 + i) / 256) and the next 17
 *                  asin((1009 + i) / 1024), the same scaling, the argument capped at 1 (the
 *                  last two are both 16384); except index 22, which is 15352 (rounding gives
 *                  15353).
 * UTIL_ATAN        +0x3ac, 257 entries i = 0..256, round(atan(i / 256) * 0x8000 / pi); except
 *                  i = 227, which is 7567 (rounding gives 7566).
 * UTIL_LAT_CIRCLE  +0x5b4, 78 entries, the circumference in metres of the latitude circle:
 *                  40075000 at the equator, falling to nothing at the pole.  It has no exact
 *                  formula.  The last entry, -505888, is past the pole: slot 0x44's byte offset
 *                  can reach it and beyond (up to +0x7fc, the end of .data).
 */

